WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.459
Film Courage: Why do you want to make movies
to help people feel less isolated?

00:00:03.459 --> 00:00:08.460
Phillip G. Carroll, Jr., Writer/Director of
THE HONEYMOON PHASE: I think one of my core

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.969
drives as a person is loneliness.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:15.360
Growing up initially in school I didn’t
have a lot of friends.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.970
I was bullied a lot.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.490
It really drove me I guess creatively.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.330
Filmmaking was the first thing that made me
cool as a kid.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.240
It was like “Oh Phil is a filmmaker.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.270
He can make movies.”

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:32.419
And it really allowed me to make friends because
kids wanted to be involved in making a movie

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:36.239
and being actors and doing cool things.

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:43.399
I really connected with that on a personal
level and knowing how hard it is feeling lonely

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:45.200
and especially as an artist too.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.960
There is so much time that you are alone.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.309
It’s very introspective.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:51.940
When you’re writing it’s just you and
your computer and you’re writing a story

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:57.300
that is solely in your head and then pretty
much through the filmmaking process even when

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.520
you’re collaborating with people it still
ultimately falls back on you as the creator

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.660
and the decision maker.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.210
Are you doing the right thing or the wrong
thing?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:14.360
So loneliness is something that drives me
as a creator and a person and movies are something

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:20.970
that I think bridges gaps in culture and when
you’re watching a movie and you’re watching

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.130
characters you are feeling something and you’re
feeling you are connected to somebody else

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:30.530
and you realize that your own personal demons
are things that everybody shares and I think

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.500
that is really important to me as a filmmaker
is to be able to connect with other people

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.390
in that way and to show people that no matter
what you are going through in life, somebody

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.560
else is going through that exact same exact
thing.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.990
Somewhere in the world somebody has the same
exact worry that you have and that you’re

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.340
not alone and that is really important to
me.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.700
Film Courage: Did any of the people that bullied
you reach out and say “I say your movie.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.320
Hey man, I’m sorry about that.”

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.350
Phil: It’s funny, I think all bullying situations
are different.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:06.300
In my situation I ended up almost becoming
friends with some of the kids that bullied

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.959
me through…elementary school was the bullying
period and then in high school when people

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:18.040
started to grow up a little bit we were able
to develop some sort of friendship and in

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:24.019
my situation I realized that I don’t think
they realized what they were doing was as

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:25.450
harmful as it was.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:31.670
I think young kids can be mean to each other
without realizing the damage that they’re

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.670
doing.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:38.609
So I don’t hold any of that against anybody
that did it because they were young, they

00:02:38.609 --> 00:02:39.680
were teens.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.829
Yes you know right from wrong but you don’t
have a concept of how much impact you’re

00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:49.240
leaving on people so I try not to hold that
against them.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.240
Film Courage: That’s good.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.879
And it helps when you grow up and have a good
right hook, too.

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:58.730
Phil: Films are my right hook.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.519
I can tell those impactful stories.

